tor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ORII TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIGA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIGEKANE MASAMICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUCHIYA MASARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIMURA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NODA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ORII, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIGA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIGEKANE, MASAMICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUCHIYA, MASARU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A heater which is easy to handle when in use, small in temperature variation and simple to produce, and which is provided with a cap (20) formed by joining and fixing together curved peripheral edges (10a) as respective peripheral edges of two semi-elliptic heater-containing sheets (10) of generally the same shape, each sheet (10) comprising a waterproof inner layer sheet (2), an air-permeable sheet (5) disposed so as to cover the entire front surface of the inner layer sheet (2) and a plurality of heating elements (3) held between and fixed by the inner layer sheet (2) and the air-permeable sheet (5) and adapted to generate heat on contact with air, the heating elements (3) being distributed over the entire surface of the cap (20), the heater-containing sheets (10) being joined and fixed together with respective inner layer sheets (2) facing inward.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce générateur de chaleur, facile à manipuler en cours d'utilisation, aux faibles écarts thermiques et de fabrication simple, a la forme d'un chapeau (20) que l'on façonne en réunissant et en attachant les bords périphériques courbés (10a) de deux feuilles semi-élliptiques (10), généralement de forme identique, renfermant le générateur de chaleur proprement dit. Chaque feuille (10) est constituée d'une feuille formant une couche interne imperméable à l'eau (2), d'une feuille perméable à l'air (5) placée de manière à recouvrir la totalité de la face frontale de la couche interne (2) et de plusieurs éléments générateurs de chaleur (3), conçus pour produire de la chaleur au contact de l'air, disposés entre la couche interne (2) et la feuille perméable à l'air (5) et maintenus par ces dernières. Ces éléments générateurs de chaleur (3) se répartissent sur toute la surface du chapeau (20). Les feuilles contenant ces éléments (10) sont réunies et assujetties par leurs couches internes (2) respectives se faisant face à l'intérieur du chapeau.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data